# Line endings
# ------------
# Git stores text as LF. On Windows the default `core.autocrlf=true` turns that
# into CRLF in the working copy — harmless for source, but not for migration SQL:
# Prisma checksums the *raw bytes* of `migration.sql`, so a CRLF checkout produces
# digests that differ from the reviewed ones in
# `prisma/migration-release-manifest.json` and from the rows already recorded in
# `_prisma_migrations`. Pinning these paths to LF keeps every checkout, on every
# platform, byte-identical to what was reviewed and deployed.
#
# `scripts/migration-ledger.mjs` verifies the manifest against the LF (Git)
# content and refuses to record checksums from a CRLF tree.
* text=auto

*.sql    text eol=lf
*.prisma text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.mjs    text eol=lf

prisma/migration-release-manifest.json text eol=lf

# Binaries Git must never touch.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.br   binary
